  "overview": {
    "text": "Alien is a 1979 science-fiction horror film directed by Ridley Scott and written by Dan O’Bannon. Its story follows the crew of the commercial spaceship Nostromo, who investigate a mysterious signal and encounter alien life. When a creature gets aboard, the crew must try to survive in the isolated ship. Sigourney Weaver plays officer Ellen Ripley. The film stands out for its claustrophobic spaceship setting, its largely unseen threat, and the unsettling creature designs of artist H.R. Giger. The British Film Institute calls it Scott’s breakthrough sci-fi horror, and the American Film Institute records that it won the 1979 Academy Award for visual effects.",
